EXT. FROZEN WATERFALL BRIDGE - DAWN

A bridge of ice spans a gorge where a waterfall hung and froze mid-fall. Blue light from within the ice. A thousand-foot drop on either side.

SIR ALARIC VENN, 40s, silver cuirass, cloak crusted with frost, edges out from the south bank. At the north end stands BRYNJOLF, 40s, bear-furred, axe on his shoulder, beard threaded with icicles.

They meet in the middle. Both stop.

ALARIC
Brynjolf.

BRYNJOLF
Alaric.

ALARIC
Cold morning for a duel.

BRYNJOLF
Cold men fight best.

ALARIC
You came alone.

BRYNJOLF
So did you.

A silence. Beneath them, the ice groans, a long deep song. Neither flinches.

ALARIC
I'd like to cross.

BRYNJOLF
I'd like the same.

ALARIC
Then you step back.

BRYNJOLF
(at the same time)
Then you step aside.

They both stop. Both smile, thinly. Alaric tilts his head. Brynjolf mirrors it.

BRYNJOLF (CONT'D)
(at the same time)
We might freeze here.

ALARIC ^
(at the same time)
We might both freeze.

Brynjolf laughs, short and sharp. He lowers the axe. Alaric lowers his hand from the sword hilt. A crack travels beneath their feet.

They freeze. The crack runs between them, glittering, and stops. They look down, then at each other.

ALARIC (CONT'D)
That was not me.

BRYNJOLF
It was not me.

ALARIC
Then who?

Above Alaric, a pillar of ice breaks loose from the cliff. Brynjolf sees it first. He lunges. He pulls Alaric down. The pillar shatters on the bridge where Alaric stood. The two men roll across the planks, and when they stop, each has a hand on the other's throat.

ALARIC (CONT'D)
(strangled)
You pulled me down.

BRYNJOLF
(strangled)
You were standing there.

They let go. Both gasp in the thin air. Wind whistles.

BRYNJOLF (CONT'D)
The bridge is breaking.

ALARIC
Then we cross together.

They help each other up. The bridge sings.
